{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.HeckeMonodromy","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Braided.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Linear","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Linear.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Basic"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands.subsingleton_of_fixed_coupling","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands.subsingleton_of_fixed_coupling","kind":"theorem","line":318,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BraidedStrands.lean#L318-L337","doc":"**A category at fixed coupling cannot carry the `q = 1` shadow.** If the tower's monodromy\nfactors through a `K`-linear category (`BraidedMonodromy`, `K` a field) and `φ(q) ≠ 1`, then a\nshadow `ε` lying over `q ↦ 1` has zero target. Reason: `q` acts on the tower through the scalar\n`φ(q)` of `End(𝟙)`, and `ε ∘ ρ` sends the unit `φ(q) − 1` of that field to `0`. The shadow needs\n`q` to vary, which a single fixed-coupling category does not provide. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands.heckeMonodromy_of_braided","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands.heckeMonodromy_of_braided","kind":"theorem","line":282,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BraidedStrands.lean#L282-L315","doc":"**Step 2 assembled from Drinfeld–Kohno and the two-strand Hecke quadratic.** If the tower's\ngenerators are the images of `σ_i = strand f n i` (`BraidedMonodromy`), `f` satisfies the\nthree-strand relation (`IsYB`; automatic for a braiding, `isYB_braiding`) and the two-strand\nquadratic `f² = (φ q − φ q⁻¹) f + 1`, then the tower satisfies the Hecke quadratic, the braid\nrelation and far commutation. The shadow `ε` lying over `q ↦ 1` is a hypothesis; see\n`subsingleton_of_fixed_coupling` for why it cannot come from the category at fixed coupling. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands.BraidedMonodromy.exists_rep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands.BraidedMonodromy.exists_rep","kind":"theorem","line":276,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BraidedStrands.lean#L276-L276","doc":"The monodromy maps, one per strand count. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands.BraidedMonodromy.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands.BraidedMonodromy.mk","kind":"ctor","line":273,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BraidedStrands.lean#L273-L273","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands.BraidedMonodromy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands.BraidedMonodromy","kind":"class","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BraidedStrands.lean#L267-L278","doc":"**Drinfeld–Kohno, as a hypothesis on a tower.** The generators of the Markov-trace tower `T`\n(over `R`) are the images of the categorical braid generators `σ_i = strand f n i` under ring maps\n`ρ_n : End(V^{⊗n}) → A` that are semilinear along `φ : R → K`. For the KZ connection this is the\ncontent of the Drinfeld–Kohno theorem (the monodromy functor is braided monoidal, so the KZ\nmonodromy of `σ_i` is the braiding acting on strands `i, i+1`). Nothing here asserts it for the\nframework's own connection (bean `qou-d0qq`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands.strand_quad","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands.strand_quad","kind":"theorem","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BraidedStrands.lean#L238-L253","doc":"**The Hecke quadratic on every strand.** If `f² = h f + 1` on `V ⊗ V`, then every `σ_i`\nwith `i + 1 < n` satisfies the same quadratic on `V^{⊗n}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands.isYB_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands.isYB_smul","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BraidedStrands.lean#L221-L226","doc":"A scalar multiple of a solution of the three-strand relation is a solution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands.braid_relation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands.braid_relation","kind":"theorem","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BraidedStrands.lean#L205-L211","doc":"In a braided category the braid generators on `V^{⊗n}` satisfy the braid relation for every\n`n`, with no holonomy computation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands.isYB_braiding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands.isYB_braiding","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BraidedStrands.lean#L196-L203","doc":"**Yang–Baxter from the hexagons.** The braiding `β_{V,V}` satisfies the three-strand\nrelation; this is Mathlib's `BraidedCategory.yang_baxter` rearranged. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands.strand_far","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands.strand_far","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BraidedStrands.lean#L159-L188","doc":"**Far commutation on `V^{⊗n}`, for any `f`.** `σ_i σ_j = σ_j σ_i` whenever `i + 2 ≤ j` and\n`j + 1 < n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands.strand_braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands.strand_braid","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BraidedStrands.lean#L133-L157","doc":"**The braid relation on `V^{⊗n}`, for every `n`.** If `f` satisfies the three-strand\nrelation, then `σ_i σ_{i+1} σ_i = σ_{i+1} σ_i σ_{i+1}` on `V^{⊗n}` whenever `i + 2 < n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands.last_pair_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands.last_pair_succ","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BraidedStrands.lean#L119-L124","doc":"The last pair is `W ◁ lastPair f V`, up to the structural isomorphism (coherence). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands.whisker_last_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands.whisker_last_two","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BraidedStrands.lean#L112-L117","doc":"The second-to-last pair is `W ◁ (f ▷ V)`, up to the structural isomorphism (coherence). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands.shiftIso","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands.shiftIso","kind":"def","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BraidedStrands.lean#L108-L110","doc":"The structural isomorphism `((W ⊗ V) ⊗ V) ⊗ V ≅ W ⊗ ((V ⊗ V) ⊗ V)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands.IsYB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands.IsYB","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BraidedStrands.lean#L103-L106","doc":"The three-strand braid relation for `f` on `(V ⊗ V) ⊗ V`:\n`(f ⊗ 1)(1 ⊗ f)(f ⊗ 1) = (1 ⊗ f)(f ⊗ 1)(1 ⊗ f)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands.strand_of_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands.strand_of_ne","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BraidedStrands.lean#L99-L101","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands.strand_last","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands.strand_last","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BraidedStrands.lean#L95-L97","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands.strand","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands.strand","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BraidedStrands.lean#L87-L91","doc":"`f` acting on the factors `i, i+1` of `V^{⊗n}` (the identity if `i + 1 ≥ n`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands.lastPair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands.lastPair","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BraidedStrands.lean#L83-L85","doc":"`f` acting on the last two factors of `(X ⊗ V) ⊗ V`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands.tpow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BraidedStrands.tpow","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BraidedStrands.lean#L78-L81","doc":"`V^{⊗n}`, nested to the left: `V^{⊗0} = 𝟙`, `V^{⊗(n+1)} = V^{⊗n} ⊗ V`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}